rship surveys - January 1977 and January 1978 - to determine how many months between February 1977 and January 1979 had Treasury bills exceeding $20,000 million. Since I only have data points for those two months, I can only definitively identify those two periods where the total nominal outstanding surpassed the threshold.\n\nLooking at the January 1977 survey, the total Treasury bills outstanding was $164,005 million, which exceeds $20,000 million. Similarly, the January 1978 survey shows $161,221 million, also above the threshold. However, I'm constrained by only having these two data points, so I cannot definitively count how many months in the full range met this criterion without additional information or interpolation between these known values.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_e359fb5ffff44cc2954e57f1","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -o \"Total amount outstanding\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1977_03_page_83.txt | wc -l"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
