ate or extrapolate the data between January 1977 and January 1978 to determine which months exceeded the $20,000 million threshold. The challenge is using just two data points to estimate monthly variations in total Treasury bills outstanding.\n\nThe Table TSO-2 provides a comprehensive view of total Treasury bills outstanding at specific points in time, while Table TSO-3 appears to break down individual issue amounts. I'll carefully examine how these tables might help me understand the monthly Treasury bills outstanding between February 1977 and January 1979.\n\nMy initial observation shows both January 1977 and January 1978 have totals above $20,000 million, suggesting a consistent trend. I'm curious about the potential insights from the monthly issue breakdown in Table TSO-3, which might reveal more nuanced details about Treasury bill distributions.\n\nI'll investigate the pattern of individual bill issues to see if they provide additional context or reveal any interesting variations in the Treasury bills outstanding during this period.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_f34d9710294d4c8c92ad2e25","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep \"Total Treasury Bills\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1977_03_page_83.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
