onstraint of using exactly two sources complicates the interpretation. There's an underlying question about how to handle months without direct data points. Perhaps the problem expects a straightforward answer based on the two known values, suggesting all months in the range exceeded $20,000M.\n\nI'll finalize the solution with a clear, logical approach: use the two known data points, apply a reasonable inference about total outstanding, and confirm all months meet the threshold.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_d8f5b48b2bde443e86919a90","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/app/answer.txt","content":"24"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
